A target of two modules that declare one import path: a's is a library package
and b's is a command. An exported function of b's command, which nothing can
import, is written under a line directive naming a file of a. It is declared in
b's package, so it is an unreachable export.

-- target/deadset.json --
{"target": {"kind": "application"}}
-- target/a/go.mod --
module example.com/app

go 1.27
-- target/a/lib.go --
// Package app is a library.
package app

// Used is the library's export.
func Used() {}
// a listing long enough to hold the line b's directive remaps here
-- target/b/go.mod --
module example.com/app

go 1.27
-- target/b/main.go --
package main

func main() {}

//line ../a/lib.go:6:1
func Exported() {}
